# Copy to .env.local if needed
# Zero-retention architecture: no server-side storage.
# Add API keys here when integrating OCR, LLM, or other services:
#
# Ask / Q&A (`/api/ask`) — Hugging Face Inference Providers (OpenAI-compatible streaming).
# Internal smoke checklist: docs/ask-team-readiness.md
# Server limits + sanitization: `lib/askGuardrails.ts` (default max question 1,000 chars; max context 100,000 chars).
# Uses the same HF_TOKEN as Summary below (one token for both).
# Default Ask model is a router chat id (see app/api/ask/route.ts). Custom Hub uploads are often NOT chat-routable;
# use an Inference Endpoint + HF_ASK_BASE_URL, or set HF_ASK_MODEL to another router chat id.
# HF_ASK_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct:cheapest
# HF_ASK_BASE_URL=https://router.huggingface.co/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
#
# Summary (`/api/summarize`) — Hugging Face Inference Providers router (OpenAI-compatible).
# Required for Summary on translate page; same HF_TOKEN powers Ask above.
# Use a fine-grained token with “Make calls to Inference Providers” (or classic token with inference scope).
# HF_TOKEN=
# Optional override if the default model is unavailable on your account or region:
# HF_SUMMARIZE_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct:cheapest
#
# --- Translate (`/api/translate`) ---
# Powered by Meta's NLLB-200 model hosted on a public Hugging Face Gradio Space
# (`Resilient-Coders/nllb-translator`). English is a client-side short-circuit
# and does not hit the upstream; Spanish and Vietnamese targets call the Space.
# Source language is fixed to English; target codes come from
# `lib/translation/nllbLanguageMap.ts` (single source of truth with the translate UI).
#
# HF_TRANSLATE_SPACE_URL is the Gradio Space base URL (no path suffix). The
# route uses Gradio's two-step call protocol: POST /gradio_api/call/translate
# to get an `event_id`, then GET /gradio_api/call/translate/{event_id} to read
# the SSE `complete` frame. The route returns 503 when the variable is unset
# or blank.
#
# HF_TOKEN is optional for Translate: the Space is public, so no Authorization
# header is sent when HF_TOKEN is empty. If HF_TOKEN is set (for Ask / Summary),
# the route forwards it as a Bearer token, which is fine for the Space.
#
# Free Spaces sleep after ~48h idle; first request after sleep can take 30–60s
# while it cold-starts. Route timeout is 180s to absorb this.
HF_TRANSLATE_SPACE_URL=https://resilient-coders-nllb-translator.hf.space
#
# --- Observability (Winnie / Team 1 eval ticket) — optional placeholders ---
# When tracing is on, each completed Ask turn posts a LangSmith run `ask-document-qa` (see `lib/langsmithAskRun.ts`).
# Default export: lengths + hashes + usage — not full question/context. For staging eval datasets only:
# ASK_LANGSMITH_RECORD_IO=true
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
# LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=multilingual-doc-assistant
# Legacy LangChain env names also work if your org uses them:
# LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=
# LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true
# LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=multilingual-doc-assistant
#
# --- Read Aloud / TTS (`/api/tts`) ---
# Powered by a Hugging Face Space running Coqui TTS. Supports English, Spanish, and Vietnamese only.
# No API key needed — the Space is a public deployment.
#
# Models hosted on the Space:
#   English    → Resilient-Coders/coqui-vctk-en  (multi-speaker VCTK)
#   Spanish    → Resilient-Coders/coqui-css10-es  (single speaker)
#   Vietnamese → Resilient-Coders/mms-tts-vie     (single speaker, Facebook MMS)
#
# Free Spaces sleep after ~48h idle; first request after sleep can take 30–60s
# while it cold-starts. Client timeout is 180s to absorb this.
#
HF_TTS_SPACE_URL=https://resilient-coders-aidoc-tts.hf.space
#
# English VCTK speaker IDs (used for gender selection). Defaults shown below.
# See http://www.udialogue.org/download/VCTK-Corpus.html for the full speaker list.
# COQUI_TTS_FEMININE_SPEAKER=p228
# COQUI_TTS_MASCULINE_SPEAKER=p226
